{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1787774729,"nonce":"a1Z7YSG0xh0CjmAZYYJMXSXcwNc=","title":"fix(web-ui): run-detail DAG zoom, attempt dropdown, activity order","message":"\u003e Imported from pull request #59 (MERGED)\n\u003e Branch: `fix/run-detail-ui-tweaks` → `main`\n\u003e Created: 2026-07-23T21:05:41Z · Merged: 2026-07-24T01:47:41Z\n\nThree small run-detail polish fixes, verified against the mock UI (`just ui-mock`).\n\n- **Reset on poll:** the auto-fit effect tracked `props.steps` directly, so every 1.2s status poll of a running pipeline (which hands back a fresh same-shape array) re-ran `fit()` and yanked the user's zoom/pan back to baseline. It's now gated on a `createMemo` of the id/service key, whose `===` guard swallows same-shape polls.\n- **Scaling the band, not the canvas:** `zoomTo()` grew `bandH`, so ＋/－ resized the entire component. The band is now a fixed viewport (sized by `fit()` on topology change); manual zoom transforms the inner canvas only and overflows/pans past the fit scale.\n\n- Restyled the attempts trigger/chip to match `.vdrop-btn` (squared surface pill, leading `⟳` emblem, caret) so the two run-detail dropdowns read as one control family.\n- Moved it to lead the coordinate stamp (left-most), aligning it under the toolbar's version dropdown.\n- Dropped the redundant trailing **\"latest\"** version tag that appeared on every attempt/step on the live view — the version segment now renders only while time-travelling (where it carries a real rerun label).\n\n- The Activity rail now shows most-recent events at the top so a live run's latest activity is visible without scrolling. `visibleEvents()` stays chronological for `StepPane`; only the rail's display copy is reversed.\n\nTypecheck clean (`tsc --noEmit`). Confirmed in the browser against the mock run: zoom holds across polls, the attempt dropdown matches the version dropdown and no longer tags attempts \"la